e,v=ev(46,'1–5 and unnumbered viniyoga/nyāsa/dhyāna','Vyāsa requests the taught thousand names. Brahmā repeats neglected worship/obstacles and subsequent proper Mahāgaṇapati worship before instruction. Ritual heading names Gaṇeśa as ṛṣi, Mahāgaṇapati/Śvānandeśa Brahmaṇaspati as deity, varied metres, gaṃ seed, tuṇḍa śakti and svāhā key; ritual aim all-obstacle destruction and divine pleasure. Limb/heart nyāsas precede red three-eyed elephant deity meditation with noose, goad, axe and reassurance, joined by Śakti, Siddhi/Buddhi. Invocation also names Lakṣa/Lābha and family/vehicle/weapon/enclosure setting, then five mental services.',[('Vyāsa',S),('Brahmā',D),('Śiva',D),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma (Upāsanā46)',T),('Mahāgaṇapati (Sahasranāma ritual deity)',D),('Svānandeśa Brahmaṇaspati',D),('Gaṃ seed',T),('Tuṇḍa mantra śakti',T),('Svāhā mantra key',T),('Siddhi (dakṣiṇā maiden)',F),('Buddhi (dakṣiṇā maiden)',F),('Lakṣa (Sahasranāma invocation)',F),('Lābha (Sahasranāma invocation)',F),('Śakti',C),('Gaṇeśa noose',W),('Gaṇeśa goad',W),('Gaṇeśa axe',W)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Booned war hymn receives explicit ritual frame.',outcome='Formula and meditation documented; heading alternate readings retained.')
rel('Gaṇeśa','rsi_of','Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma (Upāsanā46)',e);rel('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma (Upāsanā46)','ritual_deity','Mahāgaṇapati (Sahasranāma ritual deity)',e)
val('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma (Upāsanā46)','ritual_formula','Varied metres; gaṃ seed; tuṇḍa śakti; svāhā key. Viniyoga includes parenthetic deity variant Mahāgaṇapati/Brahmaṇaspati; no corrected recitation edition claimed.',e)
e,v=ev(46,'6–176','Gaṇeśa speaks a dense thousand-name hymn. Names praise forms, weapons/mounts, cosmic body, abilities, ritual seats/śaktis, mantras, script-letter sequence, traditions and numerical series. Origin/family epithets include Umāputra, Īśānaputra, Śambhu-mouth/emotion emergence, Umā-body/Gaurī-radiance/Gaṅgā emergence, Kaśyapasuta and Ṣaṇmukha-bhrātā; these are hymn epithets rather than separate enacted birth stories. Whole verse body read; individual name segmentation and every embedded kinship/śakti/weapon implication remain unextracted and prevent chapter COMPLETE.',[('Gaṇeśa',D),('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma (Upāsanā46)',T),('Umāputra (46.10)','EPITHET'),('Īśānaputra (46.11)','EPITHET'),('Śambhuvak trodbhava (46.23)','EPITHET'),('Umāṅgamalaja (46.24)','EPITHET'),('Gaurītejobhū (46.24)','EPITHET'),('Svardhunībhava (46.24)','EPITHET'),('Kaśyapasuta (46.33)','EPITHET'),('Ṣaṇmukhabhrātā (46.144)','EPITHET')],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Thousand-name teaching prescribed for war.',outcome='Hymn read; atomic segmentation/claim checking deliberately pending.')
for n in ['Umāputra (46.10)','Īśānaputra (46.11)','Śambhuvak trodbhava (46.23)','Umāṅgamalaja (46.24)','Gaurītejobhū (46.24)','Svardhunībhava (46.24)','Kaśyapasuta (46.33)','Ṣaṇmukhabhrātā (46.144)']:rel(n,'hymn_epithet_of','Gaṇeśa',e)
e,v=ev(46,'177–181','Daily Brahma-muhūrta recitation promises all worldly/otherworldly happiness. Single japa also promises longevity, health, sovereignty, courage, valour, strength, fame, intelligence/discernment, firmness, beauty/good fortune, truth, mercy, forgiveness, peace, generosity, righteousness, world-control/dialogue skill/debate eloquence, public learning, depth, brahmic radiance, high lineage/conduct/power/nobility, knowledge/discriminative knowledge/faith and wealth/grain increase.',[('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',C),('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma (Upāsanā46)',T)],story='gup2-story-tripura',outcome='General material/ethical/intellectual efficacy attached to timed daily or single recitation.')
power('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',e,v,mechanism='Text promises worldly/otherworldly happiness and listed life, character, intelligence, power and prosperity outcomes.',trigger='Daily Brahma-muhūrta recitation; single japa for181list.',notes='Prospective hymn efficacy; no named beneficiary’s completed result narrated here.')
e,v=ev(46,'182–188','Japa promises subjection of king, royal wife, royal son and minister, with targeted subject becoming servant; easy four-goal attainment; protection from Śākinī/Ḍākinī/Rākṣasa/Yakṣa/serpent fear; imperial happiness/enemy defeat; discord removal, burned-seed sprouting, bad-dream relief and angry-master appeasement; six rites/eight major siddhis/three-time knowledge; hostile ritual/army suppression; battle victory; infertility-removal/pregnancy protection. Daily recitation in a region prevents famine/calamity/evil.',[('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',C),('Targeted ruler/royal wife/son/minister','FAMILY'),('Śākinīs',C),('Ḍākinīs',C),('Rākṣasas',C),('Yakṣas',C),('Nāgas',C),('Sahasranāma daily-recitation region',L),('Burned seeds',C)],story='gup2-story-tripura',outcome='Targeted domination, protections, battle/ritual powers and regional outcomes stated.')
power('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',e,v,mechanism='Targeted japa subdues specified royal persons; grants four goals, protection, enemy/discord defeat, burned-seed sprouting, dream/master relief, six rites/eight siddhis, three-time knowledge, counterritual/army suppression, war victory and reproductive protection.',trigger='Japa, including targeted japa for subjection.',notes='Reported efficacy cluster; burned-seed sprouting literal claim retained without importing Somakānta mango completion.')
power('Sahasranāma daily-recitation region',e,v,mechanism='Absence of famine, calamities and evils.',trigger='Daily hymn reading there.')
e,v=ev(46,'189–193','Wealth does not leave a home where hymn is recited. Single japa calms listed illnesses: wasting, leprosy, urinary disorders, piles, fistula, viṣūcikā, abdominal masses/spleen/stone/diarrhoea/enlarged belly, cough/breath distress/udāvarta/pain/swelling, head disease/vomiting/hiccups/gland swelling/no appetite, vāta-pitta-kapha mixed/tridoṣa fevers, externally caused/irregular/cold/hot/one-day and other fevers, and named/unnamed disease faults. Women, Śūdras and fallen persons also attain success through single reading; parenthetical193 reading retained.',[('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',C),('Sahasranāma-recitation households','FAMILY'),('Women hymn reciters','FAMILY'),('Śūdra hymn reciters','FAMILY'),('Fallen-person hymn reciters','FAMILY')],story='gup2-story-tripura',outcome='Specific religious cure/prosperity efficacy and inclusive beneficiary statement documented.')
power('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',e,v,mechanism='Single japa calms the explicitly listed and other illness categories;193extends success to women/Śūdras/fallen persons.',trigger='Single japa/reading.',notes='Prospective hymn efficacy; no named patient’s actual cure narrated in46. Disease transliterations preserve historical categories.')
power('Sahasranāma-recitation households',e,v,mechanism='Śrī/wealth remains in house.',trigger='Hymn recitation in household.')
e,v=ev(46,'194–199','Desire-driven reciter enjoys earthly wishes and pleasant aerial vehicles/divine wish fruits, moves in desired forms/directions among Moon/Indra/Sun/Upendra/Brahmā/Rudra abodes, enjoys with chosen kin, becomes beloved Mahāgaṇapati attendant welcomed by Nandīśvara/gaṇas and cherished as son by Śiva couple; through Gaṇeśa boon becomes righteous universal sovereign remembering past lives.',[('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',C),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Moon',D),('Indra',D),('Sun',D),('Upendra (46 efficacy abode)',D),('Brahmā',D),('Śiva',D),('Nandīśvara (46 efficacy)',F),('Śiva couple in46','FAMILY'),('Sahasranāma-beneficiary aerial vehicles','VAHANA')],story='gup2-story-tripura',outcome='Desire-driven enjoyment, divine service and remembered-birth kingship promised in order.')
power('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',e,v,mechanism='Earthly/divine enjoyment, desired form/movement, divine attendant status and ultimately righteous universal kingship with previous-birth memory.',trigger='Desire-driven recitation.',notes='Prospective sequence; no enacted beneficiary or specific birth identity supplied.')
e,v=ev(46,'200–207','Desireless constant devoted reciter attains supreme yoga, knowledge/dispassion and blissful Vaināyaka abode without return. Thousand-name worship subdues kings/enemies and perfects all mantras/siddhis. Hymn called dearer than root mantra. At deity’s birth on bright fourth of Nabhas month, devotional dūrvā/name worship, prescribed libation and eight-substance homa accomplish all wishes. Recitation/reading/teaching/hearing/exposition/discussion/meditation/review/approval yield full prosperity here and beyond.',[('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',C),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Vaināyaka abode',L),('Dūrvā',C),('Eight homa substances (46 unspecified)',C)],story='gup2-story-tripura',outcome='Desireless liberation distinguished from desired enjoyment; ritual occasion and varied reception efficacy registered.')
power('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',e,v,mechanism='Supreme yoga, knowledge/dispassion, blissful Vaināyaka merging without return.',trigger='Desireless constant devoted japa.',restrictions='Desireless devotion is the specified condition for this final state.')
power('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',e,v,mechanism='Thousand-name worship subdues rulers/enemies and perfects mantras/siddhis; birth-fourth dūrvā/name/libation/eight-substance homa fulfils all wishes; many modes of reception grant prosperity.',trigger='Specified respective worship/homa/reception practices.',restrictions='Bright fourth of Nabhas month for birth festival rite; devotion/eight substances prescribed, identities not listed here.')
e,v=ev(46,'208–214','One who carries hymn even wandering freely is guarded by eight crores of Śiva-born gaṇas. Written hymn worship brings constant highest Lakṣmī; name remembrance exceeds collective donations/vows/tīrthas/sacrifices. Daily sunrise/noon/evening/three-bathing-time/constant reading brings eloquence/fame, wealth, obstacle removal, control and descendants. Poor one-pointed restrained eater practicing Gaṇeśa worship+japa four months uproots poverty accompanying seven births and gains great wealth; daily reciters gain disease-free life, pure lineage, generous wealth, fame, fresh speech/beauty, good sons and virtuous desired spouse.',[('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',C),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Śiva',D),('Eight-crore Śiva-born protecting gaṇas','ARMY'),('Written Sahasranāma',T),('Lakṣmī',D)],story='gup2-story-tripura',outcome='Protection, written-hymn worship, timed recitation and four-month poverty remedy conditions stated.')
power('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',e,v,mechanism='Carrying hymn brings protection by eight crores Śiva-born gaṇas; written-hymn worship brings Lakṣmī; daily timed/constant reading yields listed prosperity and family results.',trigger='Carrying hymn, worshipping written hymn or timed daily reading as respective conditions.')
power('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',e,v,mechanism='Uproots seven-birth poverty and grants great wealth.',trigger='Four months japa with Gaṇeśa worship.',restrictions='Poor practitioner single-minded/self-controlled, controlled food.',duration='Four months of practice; poverty said to follow seven births.')
e,v=ev(46,'215–223 (217 printed219)','Twenty-one names beginning Gaṇañjaya/Gaṇapati/Heramba/Dharaṇīdhara and ending Kāśyapa/Nandana/Vācāsiddha/Ḍhuṇḍhi/Vināyaka accompany devoted modaka offering for a year for desired success. Deity treats fixed-mind worshipful praise as thousand-name praise. Closing salutations and names beseech crossing the ocean of becoming and removal of evil. Individual name inventory remains pending, with duplicate217/219 numbering preserved.',[('Gaṇeśa',D),('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',C),('Twenty-one Sahasranāma offering names',T),('Modakas',C)],story='gup2-story-tripura',outcome='Year-long abbreviated offering efficacy closes whole read hymn.')
power('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma reciters',e,v,mechanism='Desired fulfilment through devoted modaka offerings with twenty-one stated names; focused worshipful praise equivalent to thousand-name praise.',trigger='Devoted modaka offering/name recitation.',duration='One year prescribed for offering practice.',notes='Individual twenty-one names and full1000atomic meanings remain queued rather than claiming chapter completeness.')
e,v=ev(47,'1–7','After boon/thousand names Śiva joyfully dances/roars and summons troops/gods for renewed battle. Brahmā, Kubera, Indra, Agni, Vāyu, Soma, Varuṇa and Aryamā, with Gandharvas/Yakṣas/planets/Kinnaras, bow and praise, asking when displaced gods will see enemy killed. Śiva marches gladly, inwardly contemplating Gaṇeśa, to enemy abode.',[('Vyāsa',S),('Brahmā',D),('Śiva',D),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Kubera',D),('Indra',D),('Fire',D),('Wind',D),('Moon',D),('Varuṇa',D),('Aryamā',D),('Gandharvas',C),('Yakṣas',C),('Planets',C),('Kinnaras',C),('God army','ARMY')],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Victory boon/mantra renew divine morale.',outcome='Second campaign begins with explicit inward remembrance.')
e,v=ev(47,'8–17','Spies report Śiva’s return; Tripura equips army with astras/weapons/armour, rewards fighters with cloth/garlands/ornaments/wealth, and mounts city complex. Armies clash with varied weapons and vital-piercing iron arrows, capture/kill, seize hair and behead, raising dust darkness and blood rivers. Wind clears dust, revealing dead gods, fleeing divine troops and rejoicing daityas.',[('Tripura',A),('Śiva',D),('Tripura spies','FAMILY'),('Tripura army','ARMY'),('God army','ARMY'),('Tripura three-city complex',C),('Iron arrows',W),('Armour',C)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Spies announce renewed assault and enemy mobilizes.',outcome='Second battle initially breaks god army.')
e,v=ev(47,'18–31','Vajra-bearing Indra enters, frightening daityas and crushing/killing/mutilating troops with vajra. Tripura challenges him to leave alive, promises not to strike his back, compares contest to goat/lion, then showers arrows. One enchanted arrow produces countless missiles covering sky/earth, blinding/mutilating gods/Gandharvas. Indra falls under blows, gods faint; Śiva inwardly admires Tripura’s prowess despite raging battle.',[('Indra',D),('Indra vajra',W),('Tripura',A),('Tripura multiplying arrow',W),('Gods',C),('Gandharvas',C),('Śiva',D)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Indra’s counterattack again provokes Tripura intervention.',outcome='Multiplying arrow overwhelms gods and drops Indra; Śiva assesses opponent.')
power('Tripura',e,v,mechanism='One enchanted arrow becomes countless arrows, darkens battle and wounds/incapacitates gods.',trigger='Release of enchanted arrow against divine army.')
e,v=ev(47,'32–39','Nārada arrives and advises Śiva not to worry, recalling difficult Gaṇeśa austerity, comprehensive boon and city complex unbreakable by gods with one-arrow breach exception leading to death. After his departure Śiva revives/alerts unconscious gods, remembers elephant-faced deity’s instruction recalled by adviser, and prepares deliberate killing strategy.',[('Nārada',S),('Śiva',D),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Tripura',A),('Tripura three-city complex',C),('Gods',C)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Battlefield defeat prompts last reminder of exact exception.',outcome='Gods restored to alertness; Śiva recalls divine command and acts.')
e,v=ev(47,'40–43','Śiva constructs cosmic chariot: moon/sun wheels, mountain bow, Acyuta/Viṣṇu arrow and Aśvin pair as draft horses. Printed kurūpaṃ chariot-material and yaṃtāram indīvarajaṃ driver clause remain pending exact collation; conventional Earth/Brahmā reconstruction is not silently asserted. After ācamana/inward deity contemplation he recites thousand names with one-syllable mantra, enchants fierce Pināka and Viṣṇu-form great arrow. Earth, Śeṣa, forests/mountains and celestial bodies quake/whirl; bow sound confuses gods/humans.',[('Śiva',D),('Moon',D),('Sun',D),('Cosmic Tripura-war chariot',C),('Mountain bow in47',W),('Viṣṇu',D),('Viṣṇu-form Tripura arrow',W),('Aśvin pair',D),('Pināka',W),('Gaṇeśa',D),('Single-syllable Gaṇeśa mantra',T),('Gaṇeśa Sahasranāma (Upāsanā46)',T),('Śeṣa',D)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Exact boon exception is prepared through cosmic weapon assembly/mantra.',outcome='Enchanted single arrow readied; two chariot lexical details unresolved.',status='NEEDS_REVIEW')
variant('chapter47-chariot','47.40 kurūpaṃ and yaṃtāramindīvarajaṃ are unresolved material/driver syntax. Secure moon/sun wheels, mountain bow, Viṣṇu arrow and Aśvin draft pair preserved; no remembered standard Tripura chariot supplied.',e)
e,v=ev(47,'44–47','Śiva releases great arrow, flames fill sky/earth/lower worlds. Tripura with army flees in cities, but swift arrow burns daitya and three cities. Daitya’s bodily radiance merges into Śiva while armies watch. Heavenly voice announces Śiva-slain daitya liberated. Gods/sages praise the three-eyed victor.',[('Śiva',D),('Tripura',A),('Tripura army','ARMY'),('Viṣṇu-form Tripura arrow',W),('Tripura three-city complex',C),('Tripura liberation voice',C),('Gods',C),('Sages',C)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Name/mantra-enchanted single arrow realizes boon’s exception.',outcome='Actual destruction, divine merging and liberation explicitly narrated.')
e_defeat=e
rel('Śiva','kills_and_liberates','Tripura',e);rel('Tripura','radiance_merges_into','Śiva',e)
