e,v=ev(48,'1–8','Vyāsa acknowledges Tripura-killing account and asks where Jagadambā remained, her return and date/place of burning. Brahmā dates destruction to evening full moon called Bāhulā after daytime war, explaining lamp-gifts and multiplied bath/donation/japa/homa efficacy. Nonobservance of Tripurāri festival forfeits victory/burns merit; morning Śiva worship erases night’s sins, noon worship lifetime sins, evening worship seven-birth sins.48.9 begins separate Girijā-emergence/reunion account.',[('Vyāsa',S),('Brahmā',D),('Śiva',D),('Tripura',A),('Jagadambā/Girijā in48',D),('Tripurāri full-moon festival',C),('Tripurāri-festival practitioners',C)],story='gup2-story-tripura',cause='Completed destruction prompts dating/festival aftermath question.',outcome='Full-moon evening endpoint and differentiated ritual efficacy supplied; ensuing reunion unread after48.29 fragment.')
val('Tripura','death_date','Evening Bāhulā full moon48.3, after daytime war; no unprovided month identification forced.',e)
